### PHASE 1: Security & Vulnerability Hardening (Atomic Level)
1. Rate Limiting & Abuse: Are public API endpoints protected against brute-force attacks or script spamming?
2. Data Leakage: Do API responses return clean payloads, or do they accidentally leak database IDs, user passwords, hashes, or internal system paths?
3. Input Sanitization: Is user input deeply sanitized on the backend before running queries or rendering html?
